-- REFUSE example: a case the encoding does not cover
IMPORT prelude

-- Write REFUSE where the rule stops. It type-checks at any type.
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the fee in year` year MEANS
    IF year AT LEAST 2000
    THEN 100
    ELSE REFUSE "this schedule is not encoded for years before 2000"

GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the fee is waived in year` year MEANS
    IF year AT LEAST 2000
    THEN FALSE
    ELSE REFUSE "this rule has not been written yet"

-- The branches that do not refuse answer as usual.
#EVAL `the fee in year` 2024         -- 100
#EVAL `the fee is waived in year` 2024  -- FALSE
